 "drivingQuestion": "What is R' Yehuda's reason for forty full lashes?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "each side's reading of the verse is supplied",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "makkot.22b.3",
   "daf": "22b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: אַרְבָּעִים שְׁלֵימוֹת וְכוּ׳. אָמַר רַבִּי יִצְחָק: מַאי טַעְמָא דְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה – דִּכְתִיב ״מָה הַמַּכּוֹת הָאֵלֶּה בֵּין יָדֶיךָ וְאָמַר אֲשֶׁר הֻכֵּתִי בֵּית מְאַהֲבָי״. וְרַבָּנַן? הַהוּא בְּתִינוֹקוֹת שֶׁל בֵּית רַבָּן הוּא דִּכְתִיב.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «Rabbi Yehuda says:» He is flogged with «a full forty» lashes, with the additional lash administered between his shoulders. «Rabbi Yitzḥak says: What is the reason» for the opinion «of Rabbi Yehuda?» It is «as it is written: “And one shall say to him: What are these wounds between your arms? Then he shall answer: Those with which I was wounded in the house of my friends”» (Zechariah 13:6). Rabbi Yehuda understands that this verse is referring to one with wounds from lashes administered between his arms, indicating that there is one lash administered between the shoulders. «And» how do «the Rabbis,» who hold that one is flogged only thirty-nine lashes, explain this verse? They explain that «this» verse «is written with regard to schoolchildren» struck by their teacher for laxity in their studies, and is not referring to lashes administered by the court."
  }
 ],
